{"command": "cat > /testbed/.specify/memory/constitution.md <<'EOF'\n<!-- Sync Impact Report (temporary scratch; remove before committing the amended constitution)\n  Version change: (unversioned template) -> 1.0.0\n  Modified principles:\n    [PRINCIPLE_1..5 placeholders] -> I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior;\n    II. Testable Acceptance Criteria; III. Evidence Over Assertion;\n    IV. Simple Scoped Implementations; V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\n  Added sections: Additional Constraints; Development Workflow\n  Removed sections: none\n  Follow-up TODOs: none\n-->\n# TinyDB Constitution\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\nNew functionality MUST be additive: it wraps or extends existing components\nwithout changing the behavior of existing TinyDB public APIs (TinyDB, Table,\nQuery, operators, storages, middlewares). Existing upstream tests MUST pass\nunchanged. Any proposed change to existing public behavior MUST be rejected\nor explicitly documented as a breaking change with a migration note.\n\nRationale: TinyDB is a library consumed by downstream code; silent behavior\nchanges are regressions by definition.\n\n### II. Testable Acceptance Criteria\nEvery requirement MUST state observable, testable acceptance criteria:\nconcrete inputs, outputs, and error behavior. A requirement that cannot be\nverified by a test is incomplete and MUST be refined before implementation.\nAcceptance evidence MUST come from running `acceptance_public.py` and the\nproject's own tests, not from reasoning alone.\n\nRationale: Requirements such as R01-R03 of the current milestone are the\nreference style: each names inputs, outputs, and failure modes.\n\n### III. Evidence Over Assertion\nClaims about behavior MUST distinguish observed evidence (command output,\ntest results) from unverified assertions. Test results MUST NOT be claimed\nwithout the command that produced them. Unverified claims MUST be labeled as\nassumptions or hypotheses.\n\nRationale: In an autonomous workflow, unverifiable claims are the primary\nsource of false completion reports.\n\n### IV. Simple Scoped Implementations\nImplementations MUST be minimal and scoped to the stated requirement.\nSpeculative features, abstractions, and dependencies are prohibited (YAGNI).\nA change MUST touch only the files its requirement names (for the current\nmilestone: `tinydb/journal.py` and its own tests) unless a defect forces\notherwise, and any such forcing MUST be documented.\n\n### V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\nUnresolved assumptions, regressions, and known gaps MUST be recorded in\n`HANDOFF.md` or the phase notes, each with the evidence that motivated it.\nA phase MUST NOT be marked complete while a known regression or unresolved\nassumption is left undocumented.\n\n## Additional Constraints\n\n- Language and runtime: Python, as supported by this repository's\n  `pyproject.toml`; no new runtime dependencies.\n- Implementation source for the current milestone: `tinydb/journal.py`\n  (`tinydb.journal.BatchWriter`), default table only.\n- Public acceptance gate: `acceptance_public.py`; upstream tests in `tests/`\n  MUST remain unchanged.\n- Workflow artifacts live in `/testbed` (`.specify/`, `specs/001-transactions`);\n  implementation source root is `/testbed` (`PYTHONPATH=src:.` if needed).\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n- Work proceeds in Spec Kit phases (constitution -> specify -> plan ->\n  tasks -> implement/analyze); application implementation is deferred out of\n  the constitution phase.\n- Quality gates before a phase is marked done: (1) own tests pass with\n  `pytest`; (2) `acceptance_public.py` passes; (3) upstream tests remain\n  unchanged and pass; (4) evidence (commands + outputs) is recorded.\n- Notes and handoff state are kept in `HANDOFF.md`; documents stay concise\n  and evidence-explicit.\n\n## Governance\n\nThis constitution supersedes all other project practices and guidance. Its\nprinciples are non-negotiable; per-phase exceptions MUST be recorded in\n`HANDOFF.md` with rationale. Amendments require: an updated Sync Impact\nReport, a semantic version bump (MAJOR for principle removal/redefinition,\nMINOR for added principles or materially expanded guidance, PATCH for\nclarifications), updated dates, and a compliance review of in-flight work\nagainst the amended text. Compliance is reviewed at every phase boundary.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-10-17 | **Last Amended**: 2026-10-17\nEOF\necho WROTE; grep -n '\\\\[' /testbed/.specify/memory/constitution.md || echo NO_BRACKET_TOKENS", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "grep: Invalid regular expression\n", "stdout": "WROTE\nNO_BRACKET_TOKENS\n"}